 - An `over_building` finding raised on two consecutive `validate_completion` calls, with no `finding_responses` entry answering it and no controller ruling covering it, gains a companion `major` `unaddressed_finding` with `criterion: over_building`, which moves the verdict and tells the implementer to cut the structure or answer the finding with the reason it stays. With an answer the finding stays `minor`, on that call and on the session's later ones. Structure an acceptance criterion itself mandated is reported in a finding of its own, `criterion: over_building_mandated`, addressed to the plan author: it draws no companion, and `events.jsonl` counts it separately.
 - `anti-tangent-guard`'s comment scan covers `.mjs` and `.vue` (JavaScript rules) and `.kts` (Kotlin rules). The `<!-- -->` comments of a `.vue` template block are not recognised.
 - The implementer protocol no longer calls `check_progress` optional and low-signal: the dispatch clause says to call it when the guard asks, or when drift is suspected.
+- `codebase_reference_checklist` is a field of the `validate_task_spec` envelope and of the `validate_plan` response, no longer a finding. `validate_task_spec` returns one entry per claim the reviewer could not verify; `validate_plan` one entry per affected task. It does not count as a finding, as a minor on the verdict ladder, or toward `noise_cluster`, so three unverifiable references no longer lift a clean spec to `warn`. The summary block prints it under `checklist:`, `next_action` names it, and `events.jsonl` records its length as `checklist_items`. A caller that read the checklist from `findings` / `plan_findings` by its `codebase_reference_checklist` criterion must read the new field.
 
